Input: {"question": "Which award did Carel de Haseth receive?", "documents": [{"doc_id": "d1", "text": "As Carel de Haseth stepped off the train at the Gare du Nord, the crisp Parisian air carried the whispers of history. He had always been drawn to the City of Light, where the Seine River seemed to flow with the ink of great writers and the echoes of revolutionaries. This time, however, he was not here to indulge in the romanticism of the Latin Quarter or debate the merits of existentialism at a charming café. He had been summoned to the Élysée Palace, the official residence of the President of France, for a ceremony that would recognize his dedication to the pursuit of international cooperation. As he made his way through the grand halls, adorned with the portraits of French heroes, Carel's thoughts drifted back to his early days as a young politician in the Netherlands. He had always been driven by a passion for building bridges between nations, for fostering dialogue and understanding in a world torn apart by conflict and mistrust. His work had taken him from the corridors of power in The Hague to the negotiating tables of Brussels, where he had earned a reputation as a shrewd and principled diplomat. Now, as he entered the opulent salon where the ceremony was to take place, Carel's eyes scanned the room, taking in the assembled dignitaries and diplomats. He spotted the French Ambassador to the Netherlands, a man he had worked with on numerous occasions, and exchanged a warm smile. The atmosphere was one of quiet anticipation, the soft hum of conversation punctuated by the occasional clinking of glasses. And then, the moment arrived. The President of France, resplendent in his ceremonial attire, stepped forward to confer the highest honor upon Carel de Haseth. With a dignified smile, he pinned the insignia of the Knight of the National Order of Merit to Carel's lapel, the gold and blue enamel glinting in the light. The room erupted into applause, and Carel felt 